BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grieving Spiritual Wounds
DTSTART:20260811T190000
DTEND:20260811T190000
UID:3e65e413c8197f22867911cda3747a5f@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. It is a fa
 cilitated drop-in discussion space\, with the purpose of building connecti
 on\, skill\, and resources for 2SLGBTQIA+ people navigating end of life in
  our personal lives and in our communities. Facilitated by hospital chapla
 in and writer JS Park\, join us for a care-full and open space where we ca
 n talk about losing faith and the grief of how it changes due to tragedy\,
  crisis\, and church harm. Come as you are\, and connect with others who u
 nderstand what it’s like to navigate faith and identity in difficult tim
 es. Participants are welcome to come with questions for our facilitator an
 d stories of their own experiences to share. J.S. Park is a hospital chapl
 ain\, published author\, and online educator. For nearly eleven years he h
 as been an interfaith chaplain at a 1000+ bed hospital that is designated 
 a Level 1 Trauma Center. His role includes grief support\, attending every
  death\, trauma\, and Code Blue\, and end-of-life care. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/grieving-spiritual-wounds
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
