BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baila Sáfica: Sapphic Salsa &amp\; Bachata Social
DTSTART:20260815T190000
DTEND:20260815T190000
UID:20982117a983c06bc1866d5d8853511d@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:We are back for another social dance night! Sapphics\, see you
  on the dance floor! 📍 Location: The Baby G | 1608 Dundas St W\, Toront
 o\, ON 📅 Date: Aug 15\, 2026 ⏰ Time: 7:00 PM – 2:00 AM We are back 
 with another salsa and bachata social! Join us for a night full of dance\,
  connection\, and joy! The night will begin with beginner-friendly salsa a
 nd bachata classes\, followed by a social dance where you can enjoy the mu
 sic\, practice your moves\, and dance freely. Our classes and space are de
 signed with no gender roles in mind\, so feel free to lead and/or follow\,
  switch\, and connect! 🎟 Tickets $15 (Early Bird) $20 (General Admissio
 n. These will be released once early bird tickets are sold) $25 (Support T
 icket. Choose this ticket to help us pay our instructors and DJ) $30 (Cont
 ribution Ticket. Choose this ticket to help us grow our collective and be 
 able to organize more events) NO tickets at the door. 📒 Agenda 7:00 pm-
  Doors open 7:30 pm-8:15 pm- A beginner-friendly bachata class 8:15 pm- 9:
 00 pm- A beginner-friendly salsa class 9:00 pm-2:00 am- Social Dancing 
 🌈 Please read before purchasing your ticket: Baila Safica is a sapphic 
 salsa &amp\; bachata social created to offer a safe\, affirming space for 
 sapphics to connect through dance\, music\, and community. This is a sapph
 ic-centred event. If you do not identify with the sapphic experience\, we 
 kindly ask that you sit out our events. This space is intentionally create
 d to center sapphic joy\, safety\, and community. Sapphic identity include
 s lesbians\, bisexuals\, queers\, trans women\, trans men\, fems\, masc\, 
 and non-binary folks. Our events are not for cisgender men. Sapphic identi
 ty comes in different shapes and forms\; we contain multitudes\, and it mi
 ght look different from person to person. We ask everyone to be respectful
  of the space and each other. We are creating a safe community\, and it me
 ans everyone who comes to our events belongs here\, no matter how they pre
 sent! There is no room for harassment\, bullying\, prejudice\, or any type
  of violence! Organizers reserve the right to refuse a ticket sale to thos
 e who don&#x27\;t comply with our code of conduct. Organizers reserve the 
 right to remove anyone who makes others uncomfortable during the event. We
