BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Misery Vessels
DTSTART:20260818T190000
DTEND:20260818T190000
UID:9616950c5a9f6abcd2022b4d96db0f32@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. It is a fa
 cilitated drop-in discussion space\, with the purpose of building connecti
 on\, skill\, and resources for 2SLGBTQIA+ people navigating end of life in
  our personal lives and in our communities. Come along for a hands on work
 shop where Tricia Enns shares an accessible process of creating misery ves
 sels\, objects made of paper pulp\, meant to decompose when you are ready 
 to let go. Tricia Enns (she/they) is an artist\, educator and student base
 d somewhat regularly in Tiohtià:ke (Montreal\, Canada). Their work is hea
 vily rooted in walking\, participatory\, and playful low- and high-tech pr
 actices that bring people together to create\, discuss\, and critique what
  it means to care for ourselves\, each other\, and the world around us. 
 ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/misery-vessels
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
